2. **Find wide, verify before reporting.** When available, use read-only `subagent` collectors (`subagent_type: Explore`, `model:` the READ tier value, omitted when empty) from a context not party to the code under review, and size the fan-out to the scope. Every delegate follows `references/review_rubric.md`, never writes, and never grades the overall verdict. Independent review remains the goal; if `subagent` is unavailable, perform one local pass, record that limitation, and do not repeatedly ask for unavailable tooling. Re-read the cited code for every blocker/major finding before it enters the report; downgrade or drop what does not hold up.
+++ 1
2. **Find wide, verify before reporting.** When available, use read-only `subagent` collectors with no type or model parameter, from a context not party to the code under review; size the fan-out to the scope. Every delegate follows `references/review_rubric.md`, never writes, and never grades the verdict. If unavailable, perform one local pass and record the limitation. Re-read every blocker/major citation before reporting it.
### star-code-reviewer/SKILL.md
--- 1
- **How many is the main agent's call**, sized to the work (conventions §6.2): read-only `subagent` subagents (`subagent_type: Explore`, `model:` the READ tier value, omitted when empty) run in parallel, each given the rubric, the review rule digest built at Step 1 — the same block, verbatim, for all of them — and its exact file list, returning the structured finding format in `references/review_rubric.md`. Collectors never write, never review outside their file list, never grade the overall verdict. One collector can carry a coherent scope up to roughly 50 files; past that, partition package by package in groups of 10–15, so a 60-file tree goes to four or five collectors rather than sixty. A package that hangs together may run longer instead of being cut only to hit a group size.
+++ 1
- **How many is the main agent's call**, sized to the work (conventions §6.2): parallel read-only `subagent` calls with no type or model parameter, each given the rubric, shared rule digest, and exact file list. Collectors never write, exceed their list, or grade the verdict. One can carry a coherent scope up to roughly 50 files; larger scopes partition package by package in groups of 10–15.
